libhfs from hfsutils 3.2.6, Robert Leslie, GPL-2.0-or-later.
Source: https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/h/hfsutils/hfsutils_3.2.6.orig.tar.gz
The selected C library sources are unchanged. COPYING retains the upstream
license (filename COPYING). The OS adapter and full FinderInfo catalog helper
are maintained separately in ../../src/hfs_io.cpp and hfs_metadata.c.

HFVExplorer was reviewed as a reference for direct, read/write HFS access:
https://github.com/ObsoleteMadness/HfvExplorer/tree/55a0eb7e2df20fc5d83262aabedc78712be2b9d3/src/hfs/libhfs
Its earlier hfsutils integration motivated using the standalone upstream
library. No HFVExplorer application or Windows device-driver code was imported.
The adapter opens only the selected image, bounds block I/O to its partition,
and obtains a host write lock. No physical devices or image caches are used.
